# mlx-serve — the serving engine, and nothing else.
#
# The engine choice and this exact pin come from the M8 engine bake-off
# (hack/spike/m8/findings-s5.md): vllm-mlx wins every concurrency axis, is
# Apache-2.0, is published on PyPI, and — unlike the runner-up — has a
# dependency closure that can be expressed as a hash-pinned lockfile.
#
# Nothing else belongs here. mlx, mlx-lm, mlx-metal, torch and the rest arrive
# as resolved transitive dependencies and are pinned, with hashes, in
# requirements.lock. Adding a direct requirement here changes the payload the
# image ships; regenerate the lockfile in the same commit (see README.md).
vllm-mlx==0.4.1
